{"Server-side input schema doesn't enforce uniqueness and handler comparisons are case-sensitive including blacklist, allowing duplicates or mixed-case emails to be stored and blacklist to be bypassed": 0.9687831401824951, "Team admin authorization uses AND (&&) instead of OR (||), requiring users to be BOTH team admin and team owner, which blocks legitimate team admins from adding guests to team bookings": 0.9923532605171204, "Handler filters uniqueGuests for DB insertion but passes original guests list to email sending, causing existing attendees to receive wrong email type (scheduled vs guests-added)": 0.9795404672622681, "sendAddGuestsEmails sends organizer and attendee emails unconditionally, ignoring event-type metadata flags that disable host/attendee emails": 0.9855341911315918, "Error toast handler always constructs non-empty string due to template literal, making fallback 'unable_to_add_guests' toast unreachable and showing confusing messages like 'undefined: ...'": 0.9859470129013062, "Email sending failures are swallowed with generic console.log, losing underlying error details and making production debugging difficult": 0.9658322930335999}